.TH SDL_GetGamepadSensorData 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetGamepadSensorData \- Get the current state of a gamepad sensor.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gamepad.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetGamepadSensorData(SDL_Gamepad *gamepad, SDL_SensorType type, float *data, int num_values);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The number of values and interpretation of the data is sensor dependent\[char46] See the remarks in
.BR SDL_SensorType
for details for each type of sensor\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I gamepad
the gamepad to query\[char46]
.TP
.I type
the type of sensor to query\[char46]
.TP
.I data
a pointer filled with the current sensor state\[char46]
.TP
.I num_values
the number of values to write to data\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

